s","type":"label","urls":["http://www.liesrecords.com","http://liesrecords.bandcamp.com","https://ra.co/news/81085","https://soundcloud.com/systemofsystems/paved-w-good-intentions-w-ron-morelli","http://www.soundcloud.com/l-i-e-s","http://twitter.com/LIES_News","https://www.instagram.com/lies_records","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L.I.E.S."]}},"/api/discogs/label/2773598/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2773598","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:2773598","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/2773598-Club-Queen-Records","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/424794/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"424794","image":"https://i.discogs.com/3cNl2uspbsy54SmHyBvRXBv2oqzxXUW575BUpR5ypUQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:264/w:351/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTQyNDc5/NC0xMzU4MDE5OTk5/LTk1OTEuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/UlVLYxIcAIuiq6F_atF5jNgNb9TdaurGQ5ioOPJxLCI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTQyNDc5/NC0xMzU4MDE5OTk5/LTk1OTEuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"R&B-themed compilation series released in Belgium in cooperation with the TMF music channel.\r\n\r\nNot to be confused with the similarly titled [url=https://www.discogs.com/label/4010118]Dutch series[/url] released in the Netherlands in cooperation with MTV.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:424794","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/424794-CoolSweat","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/6317/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6317","image":"https://i.discogs.com/It_693_ypHhISpZ9V8wgkesMDqg2y-N6kGUc5dyVDh4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTYzMTct/MTU0NjcxMjE3Mi02/MzEzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/RLgfprF1mjS5logk0_-z6hgkNaLGi2XImkIDjPH2kSM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTYzMTct/MTU0NjcxMjE3Mi02/MzEzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Independent Dutch label, based in Utrecht. Labelboss/DJ [a=White Delight] released 13 leftfield techno/acid/house/electro records between 1993 and 1997.\r\nThe label name was a tribute to the Chicago 'Trax' label, and since most of the talent was from the Utrecht area, U-TRAX seemed like the only possible name: tracks from Utrecht. \r\nIn 1995, the sublabel 'PHOQ U Phonogrammen' was launched for the harder / more uptempo techno & acid tracks.\r\nFrom 1997 on, U-TRAX continued as a multimedia / game translation / advertising company, until 2014.\r\nThough no records were released after 1997, the U-TRAX record label was never officially abolished.  In 2018 the label is rebooting, with some of the old releases being distributed again. In 2019, re-issues and brand new releases will follow.\r\n\r\nThe catalogue numbers missing in the series were reserved for CD releases that never saw the light of day after the label went into hibernation. Some were released on other labels later on.\r\nThese catalogue numbers have now officially been deleted and will be replaced by other releases in the future.\r\n8 UTR FDG 2: Sonar Base - untitled CD\r\n9 UTR AWAX 3: The Awax Foundation - Earwax from the AWAX files CD\r\n10 UTR AWAX 4: CultureClash - The Monster Music Radio Show CD\r\n14 UTR BISH 2: Bishop - The Hermit and the Hanged Man CD\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:6317","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":[{"id":5498,"name":"PHOQ U PHONOGRAMMEN"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/6317-U-Trax","type":"label","urls":["http://www.utrax.com","https://www.facebook.com/UTraxRecords","https://www.instagram.com/utraxquitedeepmusic/","https://www.youtube.com/user/UTRAXHQ/","https://u-trax.bandcamp.com"]}},"/api/discogs/label/821/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"821","image":"https://i.discogs.com/vMl2XlWbLiwFc15tnFdFdDhrXIwTNHLUms1TMNKeP94/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTgyMS0x/MzAwODc4NDM2Lmpw/ZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/YnKxw5pp52me5fa3hoieqaq-y_YI_lt8_yM1uZbGLTg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTgyMS0x/MzAwODc4NDM2Lmpw/ZWc.jpeg","profile":"[b]Label Code: LC 7266[/b] / [b]LC 07266[/b]. \r\n\r\nGeffen Records was started by [a=David Geffen] in 1980. Its first album was [a=Donna Summer]'s \"The Wanderer\", its second was \"Double Fantasy\", the last album by [a=John Lennon] (in collaboration with [a=Yoko Ono]). It was distributed in the US by [l90718] and internationally by [l=WEA International Inc.] throughout the 1980s. In March 1990, it was announced that David Geffen had sold the label to [l=MCA Records] however Geffen remained with WEA as distributor worldwide until 1 January 1991 when contracts expired and distribution moved to MCA or BMG. Any MCA credit is after that date in the US and after March 31, 1991, outside the US (when MCA's own deal with WEA expired). Similarly, any distribution credit for BMG is 1 April 1991 or later with the possible exception of Brazil where WEA had a distribution deal with the local BMG company. If the WEA company is referenced on a Brazilan issue, it is pre-1991.\r\n\r\nGeffen also distributed the first incarnation of [a=Rick Rubin]’s [l=Def American Recordings] through Warner Bros. Records from 1988 to 1990. At the time of its sale, it was the world’s largest independent label to have major-label distribution. In 1999, after the merger between [l=MCA] and [l=PolyGram], which created the [l=Universal Music Group], Geffen became a subsidiary of [l=Interscope Records] and was merged into the [l=Interscope Geffen A&M] division of the Universal Music Group. In 2003, Geffen Records absorbed the entire MCA Records catalog and roster when the MCA name was retired, as was [l=DGC] and [l=DreamWorks Records] the same year.\r\n\r\nIn 2017, Geffen was revitalized by Interscope Geffen A&M CEO [a=John Janick] and Geffen president [a=Neil Jacobson]. Since 2024, Geffen has been a part of Universal Music's newly-consolidated [l=Interscope Capitol Labels Group], which consists of labels belonging to [l=Capitol Records] and Interscope Records.\r\n\r\nOften credited on releases as \"Geffen\" or as a stylized \"G ball / sphere\" brand.\r\n\r\n[b]NOTE: Releases with references to both [i]Geffen Records[/i] and [i]DGC[/i] or [i]David Geffen Company[/i] as a label, should be listed under [l=Geffen Records] and [l=DGC] together.[/b]","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:821","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":1465258,"name":"Interscope Geffen A&M"},"sublabels":[{"id":162432,"name":"413 Records"},{"id":165962,"name":"DGC Records"},{"id":244557,"name":"Eleven (3)"},{"id":163922,"name":"Geffen Goldline"},{"id":37610,"name":"Geffen Home Video"},{"id":751228,"name":"Lethal Dose Records, Inc."},{"id":89094,"name":"Suretone"},{"id":48189,"name":"Zombie A Go-Go Records"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/821-Geffen-Records","type":"label","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/GeffenRecords/","https://twitter.com/GeffenRecords","https://www.instagram.com/geffenrecords/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geffen_Records","https://www.referenceforbusiness.com/history2/21/Geffen-Records-Inc.html","https://www.cvinyl.com/labelguides/geffen.php"]}},"/api/discogs/release/10903792/credits":{"cached":true,"credits":[{"id":5021249,"name":"DJ Python","role":"Main Artist","type":"artist"},{"id":1338008,"name":"Incienso","role":"Label","type":"label"},{"id":1338008,"name":"Incienso","role":"Label","type":"label"},{"id":null,"name":"Kate Stevenson","role":"Artwork By","type":"person"},{"id":92821,"name":"Simon Davey","role":"Mastered By","type":"person"},{"id":6130431,"name":"Brian Piñeyro","role":"Written By","type":"person"},{"id":6130431,"name":"Brian Piñeyro","role":"Producer","type":"person"},{"id":6130431,"name":"Brian Piñeyro","role":"Mix